course: dictionary
lesson: 2951
title: Same word, different meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their meaning depending on the words around them. Dripping is one of them. «A dripping tap can waste thousands of litres of water in a year.» Here dripping is describing the tap: it lets out small drops of water, again and again.
explain: Use the clues in the sentence. A tap that drips is leaking slowly, and the sentence says it wastes water. Check your meaning by swapping it in: «A leaking tap can waste thousands of litres of water in a year» still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Dripping has other meanings too. «Dripping wet» means extremely wet, and «dripping with sweat» means covered in a lot of sweat. Look at the words next to dripping to choose the right one.
explain: In British English, dripping can also be a noun: the fat that comes out of meat when it is roasted. A recipe that says «roast the potatoes in dripping» is not talking about water at all.
fact: Dripping can mean falling in small drops, like a dripping tap.
fact: «Dripping wet» means extremely wet.
fact: «Dripping with sweat» means covered in a lot of sweat.
fact: In British English, dripping is the fat that comes out of meat when it is roasted.
fact: «A dripping tap wastes a lot of water over days, so tell a grown-up.» In science, pupils can measure drips from a tap to learn how liquids fall under gravity.
exercise: «A dripping tap can waste thousands of litres of water in a year.» What does dripping mean here? | Very loud and noisy | *Falling in small drops, again and again | Covered in paint | Fast-flowing like a river
exercise: Ellie came in from the rain. «She was dripping wet.» What does dripping wet mean? | Happy to be outside | *Extremely wet | Cold and hungry | Slightly damp on her shoes
exercise: Mum says, «Save the dripping after the roast.» What is dripping here? | Water from the tap | Rain on the window | A small drop of paint | *Fat that comes out of meat when it is roasted
test: «A dripping tap wastes a lot of water over days, so tell a grown-up.» What should you do if you find a dripping tap? | Turn it into a game | Wait for it to stop by itself | Ignore it | *Tell a grown-up
test: After the race, Sam was ___ with sweat. Which word fits the gap? | *Dripping | Dried | Dry | Dropped
exam: A recipe says «roast the potatoes in dripping». What does dripping mean here? | *Fat that comes out of roasted meat | Covered in sweat | Small drops of water | Extremely wet
